From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:08:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: fix PA Volume dB scale

The PA Volume TLV claims -9 dB at control 0, rising 1.5 dB per step to
+37.5 dB. The control writes the gain code inverted (code = 31 -
control), and per enum wsa884x_gain code 0 is +21 dB, each code 1.5 dB
less; codes 21..31 are undocumented. On WSA8845, controls 0..17 all
give the same output, as commit b53cc6144a3f ("ASoC: codecs: wsa883x:
fix PA volume control") found for wsa883x, and control 18 is 4.5 dB
above it.

Describe -3 dB for controls 0..17, then +1.5 dB per step to +21 dB at
31. Register values are unchanged; fix the x1e80100 limit comment.

Fixes: aa21a7d4f68a ("ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: Add WSA884x family of speakers")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 10 +++++++++-
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c  |  5 +++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
index c8d3c353ec34..b1260674b62c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -1738,7 +1738,15 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget wsa884x_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SPK("SPKR", wsa884x_spkr_event),
 };
 
-static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(pa_gain, -900, 150, -900);
+/*
+ * The CSR gain field is inverted: control 31 is code 0 (G_21_DB), and code c
+ * is documented as 21 - 1.5 * c dB. As on wsa883x, codes 14..31 (controls
+ * 0..17) measure the same on WSA8845: a -3 dB floor.
+ */
+static const SNDRV_CTL_TLVD_DECLARE_DB_RANGE(pa_gain,
+	0, 17, TLV_DB_SCALE_ITEM(-300, 0, 0),
+	18, 31, TLV_DB_SCALE_ITEM(150, 150, 0),
+);
 
 static const struct snd_kcontrol_new wsa884x_snd_controls[] = {
 	SOC_SINGLE_RANGE_TLV("PA Volume", WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1,
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index 014f803f6891..7a54f6d49f00 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -89,8 +89,9 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		fallthrough;
 	case WSA_CODEC_DMA_RX_1:
 		/*
-		 * Set limit of -3 dB on Digital Volume and 0 dB on PA Volume
-		 * to reduce the risk of speaker damage until we have active
+		 * Set limit of -3 dB on Digital Volume and keep PA Volume at
+		 * control 6, the amplifier's gain floor (-3 dB on WSA8845), to
+		 * reduce the risk of speaker damage until we have active
 		 * speaker protection in place.
 		 */
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA WSA_RX0 Digital Volume", 81);
